# Trim the Docker build context — smaller context = faster builds,
# smaller images, and (most importantly) nothing sensitive sneaking
# into a layer. Keep this conservative: prefer to re-add things on
# demand rather than ship a secret.
#
# NOTE on asset directories (blog/, demo/, landing/, .well-known/,
# docs/): those are read at request time by api.py route handlers
# (blog posts, the /demo SVG, landing pages, etc.), so they MUST
# ship with the image. Don't add them here.

# ── VCS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Local credentials / env ─────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.aws/
.ssh/

# ── Python build / cache ────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# ── Virtualenvs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo

# ── Non-runtime test / bench artifacts ──────────────────────────────
tests/
bench/

# ── Databases / stateful files ──────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
data/

# ── Marketing / investor artifacts (not served) ─────────────────────
# The app doesn't read these at runtime; the repo keeps them for
# Sterling's workflow. No reason to ship them in a production image.
pitch_deck.*
haldir-pitch-deck.pdf
yc_demo.sh
design_advice.png
A16Z_SPEEDRUN_APPLICATION.md
COMPETITIVE_ANALYSIS.md
GLAMA_SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md
HOW_IT_WORKS.md
INTEGRATION_PLAYBOOK.md
INVESTOR_ONEPAGER.md
SEED_FUNDING_PLAN.md
SHOW_HN_POST.md
AGENT_DISCOVERY_LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md
DAILY_REALITY_CHECK.md
outreach_templates.md
pilot_targets.md

# ── Private working material ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The same paths `.gitignore` keeps out of the repository, listed again on
# purpose: the two mechanisms are independent, and `docker build` sends the
# *working directory* rather than the git tree, so a file git ignores can
# still land in a layer.
#
# This list had drifted from `.gitignore` — it covered the investor
# one-pagers above, but not these, every one of which sits in the repo root
# and was being copied in by the `COPY . .` at the end of the Dockerfile:
#
#   SESSION_CONTEXT.md   working notes: strategy, pricing, what is blocked
#   SOUL.md              positioning and messaging
#   FUNDING_*.md         the raise
#   USER_CONVERSATIONS.md / CONVERSATION_HISTORY.md   what customers said
#   AGENTIC_MARKET_SUBMISSION.md
#   drafts/              cold-DM and X copy — prospect names, VC targets
#   .aider*              editor transcripts
#
# `.gitignore` is the source of truth for what is private; keep this list in
# step with it and not with memory of it.
.mcpregistry_*
SESSION_CONTEXT.md
CONVERSATION_HISTORY.md
USER_CONVERSATIONS.md
SOUL.md
FUNDING_PATH.md
FUNDING_OPTIONS.md
AGENTIC_MARKET_SUBMISSION.md
OFFICE_PLAN.md
drafts/
.aider*
